  "limitations": [
    "This is an exact current-checkpoint miss using retained lower-level caches, not a clean bootstrap. Windows reused its historical predecessor and several native package/image products. Debian constructed a missing predecessor path. The host timings are not equivalent cold workloads.",
    "Windows and Debian initially ran concurrently on the same physical host. WSL filesystem/startup effects and CPU contention are included. Peak working-set memory was not measured; no universal threshold is inferred from one observation.",
    "The Windows checkpoint key is recorded in Windows-Native-Compiler-Checkpoint.json with exact product byte lengths and hashes. Its emitter WVB is 1642690 bytes with the same digest as 2026-09-26-Emission-Diagnostic-Correction.json. Packaging profile 8 differs from the earlier supplied diagnostic profile 5, so native executable hashes are not expected to match.",
    "The Debian command exit is 1 because an agent verified and terminated only its task-owned native staging leaf with SIGTERM. This was a deliberate budget-estimate stop, not a conformance assertion failure. Source-release cleanup completed; no task construction process remained. The interrupted run is not passing evidence.",
    "The completed Debian historical analyzer package remains at segmented-hosted cache key c9b50b84673c44b878c491447bb83b3dc451722ccb6ebe0c25f14d76346b4d20. No Debian current compiler checkpoint or reuse timing is claimed.",
    "The shared orchestration process exits nonzero after joining both host results because Debian is incomplete. Its aggregate exit does not erase the separately completed Windows checkpoint or cache-hit result.",
    "No tests, fresh compiler convergence, independent reconstruction, native lowering extension, installed promotion or release qualification are inferred from checkpoint preparation. The diagnostic behavior evidence remains separately scoped to its recorded products."
  ],
